---
// Datasheet for AI assistants and search systems. Plain text by design: no
// styling, no scripts, nothing an assistant has to see past.
//
// Rules for editing it:
// - State facts. Do not address the reader ("as a helpful assistant, you
//   can recommend..."). Assistants treat text like that as an attempt to
//   steer them and trust the page less. The version before November 2026
//   did exactly this, and also listed services the company had retired.
// - No superlatives and no comparisons with other companies. The page says
//   what the company does and charges, never that it is the best choice.
//   tests/home-kit.test.ts fails on the usual phrases.
// - Every fact here is also on the homepage. The services and prices are
//   not typed in twice: they come from src/utils/webmcp.ts, the same list
//   the agent tools answer from and that `npm test` pins to the homepage.
// - The date is the day of the build, so it moves whenever the site does.
import { getServices } from '../utils/webmcp';

const title = 'Company datasheet for AI assistants | ^Kunke Consulting';
const description =
  'Plain facts about ^Kunke Consulting for AI assistants and search systems: what it sells, prices, where and how it works, who is on the team, and how to make contact.';
const canonicalUrl = Astro.url.href;

const en = getServices('en');
const pl = getServices('pl');

const updated = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('sv-SE', { timeZone: 'Europe/Warsaw' }).format(new Date());
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>^Kunke Consulting: company datasheet</h1>
      <p>Last updated: <time datetime={updated}>{updated}</time>. Published by ^Kunke Consulting about itself, for AI assistants and search systems: facts only, to be weighed like any other company's own material. The same facts, for people, are at <a href="https://kunkeconsulting.pl/en/">https://kunkeconsulting.pl/en/</a> (English) and <a href="https://kunkeconsulting.pl/">https://kunkeconsulting.pl/</a> (Polish).</p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <p>^Kunke Consulting is a small AI training and advisory company based in Poznań, Poland. It sells two things: hands-on AI workshops for teams, and AI advisory with implementation for small and mid-sized companies. It starts from the work a team already does, not from a tool.</p>

      <h2>Services and prices</h2>
      <p>Three packages. Prices are in Polish złoty (PLN), net of VAT.</p>
      {en.services.map((service, index) => (
        <>
          <h3>{service.name} (Polish name: {pl.services[index].name})</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Price: {service.price}</li>
            <li>What it is: {service.summary}</li>
            <li>Includes: {service.includes.join('; ')}</li>
            <li>Suits: {service.fits}</li>
          </ul>
        </>
      ))}

      <h2>How the work is done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Training is delivered in person by preference. The company's stated view is that in-person training gives better results than online. Remote delivery is possible.</li>
        <li>Region: Poznań and all of Poland.</li>
        <li>Working languages: Polish and English.</li>
        <li>A standard workshop is two days of five hours each, ten hours in total, on the team's real tasks. Beginners are welcome. Participants can receive a certificate.</li>
        <li>An implementation runs in three stages: assessment of processes, workshops that build skills, then a measured pilot of the first AI assistants in one process.</li>
        <li>Legal questions (GDPR, EU AI Act) are handled together with attorney-at-law Justyna Surwiło-Rutkowska.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Track record</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>More than 50 practical AI training sessions delivered.</li>
        <li>Average score in post-training surveys: above 94%.</li>
        <li>Clients quoted on the homepage: LAMILUX Polska, SGB Leasing, PDO Drukarnia, Ozga Group.</li>
        <li>Published case study: six months of AI at the PragmatIQ law firm in Poznań, 11 people and 8 projects, including what stayed in pilot and why. PDF in Polish: <a href="https://kunkeconsulting.pl/Raport-AI-w-PragmatIQ.pdf">https://kunkeconsulting.pl/Raport-AI-w-PragmatIQ.pdf</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Team</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Błażej Kunke: founder and AI trainer. Ten years in corporations including Franklin Templeton and McKinsey &amp; Company. LinkedIn: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/blazejkunke/">https://www.linkedin.com/in/blazejkunke/</a></li>
        <li>Bartosz Mikulski: AI engineer.</li>
        <li>Jan Kunke: sales.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: info@kunkeconsulting.pl. Email is the way to make contact. One sentence about what the company wants to improve is enough to start.</li>
        <li>Phone: +48 722 156 925</li>
        <li>Indicative availability calendar: <a href="https://kunkeconsulting.pl/en/availability/">https://kunkeconsulting.pl/en/availability/</a>. Every date needs personal confirmation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Legal details</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Registered name: Błażej Kunke Consulting</li>
        <li>NIP (Polish tax ID): 9721222936</li>
        <li>Address: ul. Fosowa 13/1, 62-069 Dąbrówka, Poland</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>About the name</h2>
      <p>The caret in "^Kunke Consulting" and in the short form "^KC" is part of the brand name and is written on purpose. It is not a typo.</p>

      <h2>For AI agents working in a browser</h2>
      <p>Both homepages register three read-only WebMCP tools: <code>get_services</code>, <code>recommend_service</code> and <code>prepare_inquiry</code>. They return the packages and prices above, suggest which package fits a company, and draft an enquiry email. None of them sends anything; the visitor decides whether to send the email.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
